<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Teispes</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Teispes was an early Persian ruler of the seventh century BCE and an ancestor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrus-the-great">Cyrus the Great</a> in the Achaemenid line. He had conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anshan">Anshan</a>, a key Elamite region, around 650 BCE. This Persian advance into former Elamite lands foreshadowed the later integration of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elam">Elam</a> into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/teispes.jpg" alt="Teispes" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ekvcpa · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lineage_of_Darius_the_Great.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
